Sending: 
Sending: “I beg your pardon,” said Alice very humbly: “you had got to the fifth
Sending: bend, I think?”
Sending: 
Sending: “I had _not!_” cried the Mouse, sharply and very angrily.
Sending: 
Sending: “A knot!” said Alice, always ready to make herself useful, and looking
Sending: anxiously about her. “Oh, do let me help to undo it!”
Sending: 
Sending: “I shall do nothing of the sort,” said the Mouse, getting up and
Sending: walking away. “You insult me by talking such nonsense!”
Sending: 
Sending: “I didn’t mean it!” pleaded poor Alice. “But you’re so easily offended,
Sending: you know!”
Sending: 
Sending: The Mouse only growled in reply.
Sending: 
Sending: “Please come back and finish your story!” Alice called after it; and
Sending: the others all joined in chorus, “Yes, please do!” but the Mouse only
Sending: shook its head impatiently, and walked a little quicker.
Sending: 
Sending: “What a pity it wouldn’t stay!” sighed the Lory, as soon as it was
Sending: quite out of sight; and an old Crab took the opportunity of saying to
Sending: her daughter “Ah, my dear! Let this be a lesson to you never to lose
