Sending: snappishly. “You’re enough to try the patience of an oyster!”
Sending: 
Sending: “I wish I had our Dinah here, I know I do!” said Alice aloud,
Sending: addressing nobody in particular. “She’d soon fetch it back!”
Sending: 
Sending: “And who is Dinah, if I might venture to ask the question?” said the
Sending: Lory.
Sending: 
Sending: Alice replied eagerly, for she was always ready to talk about her pet:
Sending: “Dinah’s our cat. And she’s such a capital one for catching mice you
Sending: can’t think! And oh, I wish you could see her after the birds! Why,
Sending: she’ll eat a little bird as soon as look at it!”
