Sending: 
Sending: 
Sending: “That is not said right,” said the Caterpillar.
Sending: 
Sending: “Not _quite_ right, I’m afraid,” said Alice, timidly; “some of the
Sending: words have got altered.”
Sending: 
Sending: “It is wrong from beginning to end,” said the Caterpillar decidedly,
Sending: and there was silence for some minutes.
Sending: 
Sending: The Caterpillar was the first to speak.
Sending: 
Sending: “What size do you want to be?” it asked.
Sending: 
Sending: “Oh, I’m not particular as to size,” Alice hastily replied; “only one
Sending: doesn’t like changing so often, you know.”
Sending: 
Sending: “I _don’t_ know,” said the Caterpillar.
Sending: 
Sending: Alice said nothing: she had never been so much contradicted in her life
Sending: before, and she felt that she was losing her temper.
Sending: 
Sending: “Are you content now?” said the Caterpillar.
