Sending: grow shorter.”
Sending: 
Sending: “One side of _what?_ The other side of _what?_” thought Alice to
Sending: herself.
Sending: 
Sending: “Of the mushroom,” said the Caterpillar, just as if she had asked it
Sending: aloud; and in another moment it was out of sight.
Sending: 
Sending: Alice remained looking thoughtfully at the mushroom for a minute,
Sending: trying to make out which were the two sides of it; and as it was
Sending: perfectly round, she found this a very difficult question. However, at
Sending: last she stretched her arms round it as far as they would go, and broke
Sending: off a bit of the edge with each hand.
Sending: 
Sending: “And now which is which?” she said to herself, and nibbled a little of
Sending: the right-hand bit to try the effect: the next moment she felt a
Sending: violent blow underneath her chin: it had struck her foot!
Sending: 
Sending: She was a good deal frightened by this very sudden change, but she felt
Sending: that there was no time to be lost, as she was shrinking rapidly; so she
Sending: set to work at once to eat some of the other bit. Her chin was pressed
Sending: so closely against her foot, that there was hardly room to open her
Sending: mouth; but she did it at last, and managed to swallow a morsel of the
Sending: lefthand bit.
Sending: 
