Sending: hedges,” the Pigeon went on, without attending to her; “but those
Sending: serpents! There’s no pleasing them!”
Sending: 
Sending: Alice was more and more puzzled, but she thought there was no use in
Sending: saying anything more till the Pigeon had finished.
Sending: 
Sending: “As if it wasn’t trouble enough hatching the eggs,” said the Pigeon;
