Sending: “It’s a Cheshire cat,” said the Duchess, “and that’s why. Pig!”
Sending: 
Sending: She said the last word with such sudden violence that Alice quite
Sending: jumped; but she saw in another moment that it was addressed to the
Sending: baby, and not to her, so she took courage, and went on again:—
Sending: 
Sending: “I didn’t know that Cheshire cats always grinned; in fact, I didn’t
Sending: know that cats _could_ grin.”
Sending: 
Sending: “They all can,” said the Duchess; “and most of ’em do.”
