Sending: As soon as she had made out the proper way of nursing it, (which was to
Sending: twist it up into a sort of knot, and then keep tight hold of its right
Sending: ear and left foot, so as to prevent its undoing itself,) she carried it
Sending: out into the open air. “If I don’t take this child away with me,”
