Sending: murder to leave it behind?” She said the last words out loud, and the
Sending: little thing grunted in reply (it had left off sneezing by this time).
Sending: “Don’t grunt,” said Alice; “that’s not at all a proper way of
Sending: expressing yourself.”
Sending: 
Sending: The baby grunted again, and Alice looked very anxiously into its face
Sending: to see what was the matter with it. There could be no doubt that it had
Sending: a _very_ turn-up nose, much more like a snout than a real nose; also
Sending: its eyes were getting extremely small for a baby: altogether Alice did
Sending: not like the look of the thing at all. “But perhaps it was only
Sending: sobbing,” she thought, and looked into its eyes again, to see if there
Sending: were any tears.
Sending: 
Sending: No, there were no tears. “If you’re going to turn into a pig, my dear,”
