Sending: tone though), “I won’t have any pepper in my kitchen _at all_. Soup
Sending: does very well without—Maybe it’s always pepper that makes people
Sending: hot-tempered,” she went on, very much pleased at having found out a new
Sending: kind of rule, “and vinegar that makes them sour—and camomile that makes
Sending: them bitter—and—and barley-sugar and such things that make children
Sending: sweet-tempered. I only wish people knew _that_: then they wouldn’t be
Sending: so stingy about it, you know—”
