Sending: “And how many hours a day did you do lessons?” said Alice, in a hurry
Sending: to change the subject.
Sending: 
Sending: “Ten hours the first day,” said the Mock Turtle: “nine the next, and so
Sending: on.”
Sending: 
Sending: “What a curious plan!” exclaimed Alice.
Sending: 
Sending: “That’s the reason they’re called lessons,” the Gryphon remarked:
Sending: “because they lessen from day to day.”
Sending: 
Sending: This was quite a new idea to Alice, and she thought it over a little
Sending: before she made her next remark. “Then the eleventh day must have been
Sending: a holiday?”
Sending: 
Sending: “Of course it was,” said the Mock Turtle.
Sending: 
Sending: “And how did you manage on the twelfth?” Alice went on eagerly.
